# Gym4Me Product Decisions

## Auth & roles

- Users may hold multiple roles (`User.roles`).
- JWT must include `activeRole`; **authorization uses `activeRole` only**. `roles` is for UI switcher.
- Role switch: `POST /account/auth/switch-role` → validate membership → new token pair → revoke prior refresh.
- One mobile app with an in-app role switcher (athlete / coach / owner).

## Club staff

- Fine-grained permissions via `PermissionDefinition` keys (`bookings.create`, `finance.read`, …).
- Named staff roles are presets only; final grants are per staff member.

## Booking

- Independent calendars/capacity for space, session, coach, class.
- Recurring bookings use `recurringGroupId`; cancel single occurrence or series from date.
- Full `BookingStatus`: PENDING, AWAITING_PAYMENT, CONFIRMED, CHECKED_IN, COMPLETED, CANCELLED, NO_SHOW, REFUND_REQUESTED, REFUNDED, REJECTED.

## Privacy

- Metrics, progress photos, meal plans default to PRIVATE; enforce in API.
- Levels: PUBLIC | FOLLOWERS | COACH_ONLY | PRIVATE.

## Money

- Keep platform subscriptions and club memberships as separate domains.
- Immutable double-entry Ledger is source of truth; wallet balance is a derived cache.
- Split every payment: amount − discount − tax − provider share − platform fee − gateway fee = net settle.

## Integrations

- SMS: Kavenegar behind `SmsService` (`SMS_PROVIDER=kavenegar|mock`).
- Payments: Zarinpal behind `PaymentGatewayService` (`PAYMENT_PROVIDER=zarinpal|mock`).

## Apps

- `apps/api` = single source of truth; `apps/mobile` = multi-role app; `apps/admin` = ops; `apps/website` = public/SEO.
- Runtime DB is **MongoDB (Mongoose)** under `apps/api/src/schemas`. No PostgreSQL migration.
- Follow locked decisions in `docs/product/`.

## Delivery & tracking

- Bootstrap: version-neutral `GET /api/app-config/bootstrap` with independent `schemaVersion`.
- `/api/v2` only for breaking changes; keep at least two API generations for ≥6 months.
- Feature flags activate pre-bundled code only — never authorization.
- Athlete data grants are per-scope/time-bound with immediate query-time revoke.
- Metric reminders default off (opt-in). Health samples retained after disconnect until explicit delete.